[38;5;252m[1m## Bugs the differential testing found and I fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [38;5;10merror.rs[0m — Rust's [38;5;10mb"\0"[0m is 1 byte where C's [38;5;10m"\0"[0m is 2; the message-counting loop went out of bounds.[0m[0m
2. [38;5;10mcompile_parse.rs[0m — a duplicated literal emit made every escape ([38;5;10m\x41[0m, [38;5;10m\101[0m, [38;5;10m\cA[0m, [38;5;10m\e[0m, …) produce two characters.[0m[0m
3. [38;5;10mcompile_branch.rs[0m — the [38;5;10mbralink[0m chain-closing loop sat inside the real-pass branch, so the length pass under-counted [38;5;10m(X){0,n}[0m and every such pattern failed with an internal code-overflow error.[0m[0m
4. [38;5;10mstudy.rs[0m — C's [38;5;10mcase OP_XCLASS:[0m falls through into [38;5;10mcase OP_NCLASS:[0m; the Rust gated that block on [38;5;10m*tcode == OP_NCLASS[0m, corrupting [38;5;10mstart_bitmap[0m (visible through [38;5;10mpcre2_serialize_encode[0m).[0m[0m
